IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap5-s2025-ab`

-- LAYER 1: section 2025(g) and (h)(1)(A)-(E), (h)(2)-(5): cost sharing for computerization, and funding of employment and training programs
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025; lines 2086-2153 and 2279-2324 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a share is a fraction (50 percent is 0.50).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says, NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).
-- Answers section 2015 supplies (the exceptions, waiver and exemption of section 2015(o), the dependent care payment of
-- section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II)) are asked as inputs named for the answering section (SEAMS.md).

-- s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II): the groups at which a reallocation may be targeted, and any other.
DECLARE `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) group` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(aa) individuals 50 years of age or older`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(bb) formerly incarcerated individuals`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(cc) individuals participating in a substance abuse treatment program`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(dd) homeless individuals`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(ee) people with disabilities seeking to enter the workforce`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(ff) other individuals with substantial barriers to employment`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(gg) households facing multi-generational poverty`
    `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) any other group`

-- s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv): the reporting measures the text lists, and any other.
DECLARE `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) measure` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv)(I) percentage and number of participants in unsubsidized employment after the services`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv)(II) percentage and number of participants who obtain a recognized credential`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv)(III) percentage and number of participants in an education or training program intended to lead to a credential or employment`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv)(IV) measures developed by each State agency to assess skills acquisition`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv)(V) other indicators approved by the Secretary`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) any other measure`

-- s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv): the information the Secretary may require for a State receiving additional allocations, and any other.
DECLARE `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) information` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv)(I) a report for each fiscal year of the numbers who meet the conditions, are offered a position, and participate`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv)(II) a description of the programs the State agency uses and their availability`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv)(III) any additional information the Secretary determines appropriate`
    `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) any other information`

§ `s 2025(g) Cost sharing for computerization`

-- src:2089 | (A) planning, design, development, or installation of 1 or more automatic data processing and information retrieval systems that the Secretary determines—
-- src:2090 | (i) would assist in meeting the requirements of this chapter;
-- src:2091 | (ii) meet such conditions as the Secretary prescribes;
-- src:2092 | (iii) are likely to provide more efficient and effective administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- src:2093 | (iv) would be compatible with other systems used in the administration of State programs, including the program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.);
-- src:2094 | (v) would be tested adequately before and after implementation, including a requirement that—
-- src:2095 | (I) such testing shall be accomplished through pilot projects in limited areas for major systems changes (as determined under rules promulgated by the Secretary);
-- src:2096 | (II) each pilot project described in subclause (I) that is carried out before the implementation of a system shall be conducted in a live-production environment; and
-- src:2097 | (III) the data resulting from each pilot project carried out under this clause shall be thoroughly evaluated before the Secretary approves the system to be implemented more broadly;
-- src:2098 | (vi) would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan for—
-- src:2099 | (I) continuous updating to reflect changed policy and circumstances; and
-- src:2100 | (II) testing the effect of the system on access for eligible households and on payment accuracy; and
-- src:2101 | (vii) would be accessible by the Secretary for inspection and audit under section 2020(a)(3)(B) of this title; and
@ref s 2025(g)(1)(A) the systems that qualify (src:2089-2101)
GIVEN `it would assist in meeting the requirements of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it meets such conditions as the Secretary prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is likely to provide more efficient and effective administration of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would be compatible with other systems used in the administration of State programs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would be tested adequately before and after implementation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it would be accessible by the Secretary for inspection and audit under section 2020(a)(3)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the system has these qualities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(g)(1)(A) the planning, design, development or installation of the system qualifies for payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "automatic data processing and information retrieval systems that the Secretary determines— (i) would assist in meeting the requirements of this chapter"
        IF (NOT (`it would assist in meeting the requirements of this chapter`
            AND `it meets such conditions as the Secretary prescribes`
            AND `it is likely to provide more efficient and effective administration of the program`
            AND `it would be compatible with other systems used in the administration of State programs`
            AND `it would be accessible by the Secretary for inspection and audit under section 2020(a)(3)(B)`))
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(v) would be tested adequately before and after implementation"
        IF `it would be tested adequately before and after implementation` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `it would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer to clause (v) or clause (vi) was not supplied
        IF `it would be tested adequately before and after implementation` EQUALS NOTHING OR `it would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that the system has these qualities`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "systems that the Secretary determines"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2094 | (v) would be tested adequately before and after implementation, including a requirement that—
-- src:2095 | (I) such testing shall be accomplished through pilot projects in limited areas for major systems changes (as determined under rules promulgated by the Secretary);
-- src:2096 | (II) each pilot project described in subclause (I) that is carried out before the implementation of a system shall be conducted in a live-production environment; and
-- src:2097 | (III) the data resulting from each pilot project carried out under this clause shall be thoroughly evaluated before the Secretary approves the system to be implemented more broadly;
@ref s 2025(g)(1)(A)(v) tested adequately (src:2094-2097)
GIVEN `the testing is adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `testing is accomplished through pilot projects in limited areas for major systems changes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each pilot project carried out before implementation is conducted in a live-production environment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data resulting from each pilot project is thoroughly evaluated before the Secretary approves the system for broader implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(g)(1)(A)(v) the system would be tested adequately before and after implementation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the testing is adequate`
            AND `testing is accomplished through pilot projects in limited areas for major systems changes`
            AND `each pilot project carried out before implementation is conducted in a live-production environment`
            AND `the data resulting from each pilot project is thoroughly evaluated before the Secretary approves the system for broader implementation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "would be tested adequately before and after implementation, including a requirement that"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2098 | (vi) would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan for—
-- src:2099 | (I) continuous updating to reflect changed policy and circumstances; and
-- src:2100 | (II) testing the effect of the system on access for eligible households and on payment accuracy; and
@ref s 2025(g)(1)(A)(vi) an adequate plan (src:2098-2100)
GIVEN `the plan is adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for continuous updating to reflect changed policy and circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for testing the effect of the system on access for eligible households and on payment accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(g)(1)(A)(vi) the system would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan is adequate` AND `it provides for continuous updating to reflect changed policy and circumstances` AND `it provides for testing the effect of the system on access for eligible households and on payment accuracy` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "would be operated in accordance with an adequate plan for"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2102 | (B) operation of 1 or more automatic data processing and information retrieval systems that the Secretary determines may continue to be operated in accordance with clauses (i) through (vii) of subparagraph (A).
@ref s 2025(g)(1)(B) operation of the systems (src:2102)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the system may continue to be operated in accordance with clauses (i) through (vii) of subparagraph (A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(g)(1)(B) the operation of the system qualifies for payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that the system may continue to be operated in accordance with clauses (i) through (vii) of subparagraph (A)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "systems that the Secretary determines may continue to be operated in accordance with clauses (i) through (vii)"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2105 | (A) is reimbursed for the costs under any other Federal program; or
-- src:2106 | (B) uses the systems for purposes not connected with the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2025(g)(2) limitation (src:2105-2106)
GIVEN `costs incurred by the State agency, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `costs reimbursed under any other Federal program, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `costs of the systems used for purposes not connected with the program, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(g)(2) the costs on which the Secretary may make payments after the limitation` MEANS
    -- The two kinds of cost are taken as separate costs, as the caller states them; the text does not say how an overlap is counted (NOTES.md, fork F-8).
    max 0 (`costs incurred by the State agency, in dollars` MINUS `costs reimbursed under any other Federal program, in dollars` MINUS `costs of the systems used for purposes not connected with the program, in dollars`)

-- "the amount provided under subsection (a)(6)" is read as the share of subsection (a) times the costs (NOTES.md, fork F-7).
-- src:2088 | Except as provided in paragraph (2), the Secretary is authorized to pay to each State agency the amount provided under subsection (a)(6) for the costs incurred by the State agency in the—
@ref s 2025(g)(1) the amount provided under subsection (a)(6) (src:2088)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `costs incurred by the State agency, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `costs reimbursed under any other Federal program, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `costs of the systems used for purposes not connected with the program, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the system qualifies for payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(g)(1) the amount the Secretary is authorized to pay for the costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the system qualifies for payment`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 2025(a) the share of administrative costs the Secretary is authorized to pay` `fiscal year`
        WHEN JUST share THEN JUST (share TIMES `s 2025(g)(2) the costs on which the Secretary may make payments after the limitation` `costs incurred by the State agency, in dollars` `costs reimbursed under any other Federal program, in dollars` `costs of the systems used for purposes not connected with the program, in dollars`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 2025(a) states no share for that fiscal year
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the payment is for costs in the systems "that the Secretary determines" qualify under subparagraph (A) or (B)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(h)(1) Funding of employment and training programs: amounts, allocation, reallocation`

-- src:2110 | To carry out employment and training programs, the Secretary shall reserve for allocation to State agencies, to remain available for 24 months, from funds made available for each fiscal year under section 2027(a)(1) of this title, $103,900,000 for each fiscal year.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(A) $103,900,000 for each fiscal year, available for 24 months (src:2110)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(1)(A) the amount the Secretary shall reserve for each fiscal year, in dollars` MEANS
    103_900_000

@ref s 2025(h)(1)(A) to remain available for 24 months (src:2110)
GIVEN `date the funds are reserved for allocation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(h)(1)(A) the last day the funds remain available` MEANS
    -- Fork F-13 in NOTES.md: "to remain available for 24 months" is read as ending on the same day of the month 24 months after the date the funds are reserved.
    `add months` `date the funds are reserved for allocation` 24

-- src:2112 | Funds made available under subparagraph (A) shall be made available to and reallocated among State agencies under a reasonable formula that—
-- src:2113 | (i) is determined and adjusted by the Secretary; and
-- src:2114 | (ii) takes into account the number of individuals who are not exempt from the work requirement under section 2015(o) of this title.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(B) allocation under a reasonable formula (src:2112-2114)
GIVEN `the formula is determined and adjusted by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it takes into account the number of individuals who are not exempt from the work requirement under section 2015(o)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the formula is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(B) the allocation is made under a formula of the kind required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the formula is determined and adjusted by the Secretary` AND `it takes into account the number of individuals who are not exempt from the work requirement under section 2015(o)` AND `the formula is reasonable` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made available to and reallocated among State agencies under a reasonable formula that"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2117 | If a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year under subparagraph (B), the Secretary, subject to clauses (ii) through (v), shall reallocate the unexpended funds to other States (during the fiscal year or the subsequent fiscal year) as the Secretary considers appropriate and equitable.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(i) reallocation of unexpended funds (src:2117)
GIVEN `the State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated for the fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unexpended funds, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(i) the unexpended funds the Secretary shall reallocate to other States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated for the fiscal year` THEN JUST `unexpended funds, in dollars`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a State agency will not expend all of the funds allocated to the State agency for a fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2119 | The Secretary shall collect such information as the Secretary determines to be necessary about the expenditures and anticipated expenditures by the State agencies of the funds initially allocated to the State agencies under subparagraph (A) to make reallocations of unexpended funds under clause (i) within a timeframe that allows each State agency to which funds are reallocated at least 270 days to expend the reallocated funds.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(ii) timing: at least 270 days (src:2119)
GIVEN `days the State agency receiving reallocated funds has to expend them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(ii) the reallocation allows the State agency the time required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `days the State agency receiving reallocated funds has to expend them` AT LEAST 270 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a timeframe that allows each State agency to which funds are reallocated at least 270 days to expend the reallocated funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2121 | The Secretary shall ensure that all State agencies have an opportunity to obtain reallocated funds.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iii) opportunity (src:2121)
GIVEN `all State agencies have had an opportunity to obtain reallocated funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iii) every State agency has had an opportunity to obtain reallocated funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `all State agencies have had an opportunity to obtain reallocated funds` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall ensure that all State agencies have an opportunity to obtain reallocated funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2125 | (aa) Subject to items (bb) and (cc), not less than 50 percent shall be reallocated to State agencies requesting such funds to conduct employment and training programs and activities for which such State agencies had previously received funding under subparagraph (F)(viii) that the Secretary determines have the most demonstrable impact on the ability of participants to find and retain employment that leads to increased household income and reduced reliance on public assistance.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(aa) not less than 50 percent (src:2125)
GIVEN `total reallocated, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `reallocated under subclause (I), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I) the amount reallocated under subclause (I) meets the minimum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reallocated under subclause (I), in dollars` AT LEAST (`total reallocated, in dollars` TIMES 0.50) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not less than 50 percent shall be reallocated to State agencies requesting such funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2127 | (AA) project results from the independent evaluations conducted under subparagraph (F)(vii)(I); or
-- src:2128 | (BB) if the project results from the independent evaluations conducted under subparagraph (F)(vii)(I) are not yet available, the reports under subparagraph (F)(vii)(II) or other information relating to performance of the programs and activities funded under subparagraph (F)(viii).
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(bb) the basis of the determination (src:2127-2128)
GIVEN `project results from the independent evaluations are available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is based on those project results` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is based on the reports or other information relating to the performance of the programs and activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(bb) the determination is based on what the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `project results from the independent evaluations are available` THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the determination is based on those project results` THEN JUST TRUE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall base the determination under item (aa) on— (AA) project results from the independent evaluations"
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            BRANCH
                IF `the determination is based on the reports or other information relating to the performance of the programs and activities` THEN JUST TRUE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the project results from the independent evaluations conducted under subparagraph (F)(vii)(I) are not yet available, the reports under subparagraph (F)(vii)(II) or other information"
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2129 | (cc) Employment and training activities funded under this subclause are not subject to subparagraph (F)(vii), but are subject to monitoring under paragraph (h)(5).
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(cc) not subject to subparagraph (F)(vii), subject to monitoring (src:2129)
GIVEN `the activities are funded under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(cc) the activities are subject to the evaluation of subparagraph (F)(vii)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Employment and training activities funded under this subclause are not subject to subparagraph (F)(vii)"
        IF `the activities are funded under subclause (I)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption is for activities "funded under this subclause"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(cc) subject to monitoring under paragraph (h)(5) (src:2129)
GIVEN `the activities are funded under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(I)(cc) the activities are subject to monitoring under paragraph (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the activities are funded under subclause (I)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the monitoring is of activities "funded under this subclause"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2130 | (II) Not less than 30 percent shall be reallocated to State agencies requesting such funds to implement or continue employment and training programs and activities under section 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) of this title that the Secretary determines have the most demonstrable impact on the ability of participants to find and retain employment that leads to increased household income and reduced reliance on public assistance, including programs and activities that are targeted to—
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) not less than 30 percent (src:2130)
GIVEN `total reallocated, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `reallocated under subclause (II), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) the amount reallocated under subclause (II) meets the minimum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reallocated under subclause (II), in dollars` AT LEAST (`total reallocated, in dollars` TIMES 0.30) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not less than 30 percent shall be reallocated to State agencies requesting such funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2131 | (aa) individuals 50 years of age or older;
-- src:2132 | (bb) formerly incarcerated individuals;
-- src:2133 | (cc) individuals participating in a substance abuse treatment program;
-- src:2134 | (dd) homeless individuals;
-- src:2135 | (ee) people with disabilities seeking to enter the workforce;
-- src:2136 | (ff) other individuals with substantial barriers to employment; or
-- src:2137 | (gg) households facing multi-generational poverty, to support employment and workforce participation through an integrated and family-focused approach in providing supportive services.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II)(aa)-(gg) targeted groups (src:2131-2137)
GIVEN group IS A `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) the group is one the programs and activities are targeted to` MEANS
    CONSIDER group
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including programs and activities that are targeted to" the seven listed groups
    WHEN `s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(II) any other group` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2138 | (III) The Secretary shall reallocate any remaining funds available under this subparagraph, to State agencies requesting such funds to use for employment and training programs and activities that the Secretary determines have the most demonstrable impact on the ability of participants to find and retain employment that leads to increased household income and reduced reliance on public assistance under section 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) of this title.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(III) any remaining funds (src:2138)
GIVEN `total reallocated, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `reallocated under subclause (I), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `reallocated under subclause (II), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(iv)(III) the remaining funds to be reallocated` MEANS
    max 0 (`total reallocated, in dollars` MINUS `reallocated under subclause (I), in dollars` MINUS `reallocated under subclause (II), in dollars`)

-- src:2140 | In reallocating funds under this subparagraph, a State agency that receives reallocated funds under clause (iv)(I) may also be considered for reallocated funding under clause (iv)(II).
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(C)(v) consideration (src:2140)
GIVEN `the State agency receives reallocated funds under clause (iv)(I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(C)(v) the State agency may also be considered for funding under clause (iv)(II)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency receives reallocated funds under clause (iv)(I)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a State agency that receives reallocated funds under clause (iv)(I) may also be considered"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2142 | Notwithstanding subparagraph (B), the Secretary shall ensure that each State agency operating an employment and training program shall receive not less than $100,000 for each fiscal year.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(D) minimum allocation of $100,000 (src:2142)
GIVEN `the State agency operates an employment and training program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `allocation for the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(D) the allocation meets the minimum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each State agency operating an employment and training program"
        IF (NOT `the State agency operates an employment and training program`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `allocation for the fiscal year, in dollars` AT LEAST 100_000 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall receive not less than $100,000 for each fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2145 | In addition to the allocations under subparagraph (A), from funds made available under section 2027(a)(1) of this title, the Secretary shall allocate not more than $20,000,000 for each fiscal year to reimburse a State agency that is eligible under clause (ii) for the costs incurred in serving members of households receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits who—
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(E)(i) not more than $20,000,000 for each fiscal year (src:2145)
GIVEN `amount allocated for the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(E)(i) the additional allocation is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `amount allocated for the fiscal year, in dollars` AT MOST 20_000_000 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall allocate not more than $20,000,000 for each fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2146 | (I) are not eligible for an exception under section 2015(o)(3) of this title; and
-- src:2147 | (II) are placed in and comply with a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2) of this title.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(E)(i)(I)-(II) the members whose costs are reimbursed (src:2146-2147)
GIVEN `the State agency is eligible under clause (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member's household receives program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(o)(3) the individual is eligible for an exception` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the member is placed in and complies with a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(E)(i) the costs of serving the member may be reimbursed from the additional allocation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency is eligible under clause (ii)`
            AND `the member's household receives program benefits`
            AND `s 2015(o)(3) the individual is eligible for an exception` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `the member is placed in and complies with a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the costs incurred in serving members of households receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits who" are "not eligible for an exception" and are "placed in and comply with a program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2149 | To be eligible for an additional allocation under clause (i), a State agency shall make and comply with a commitment to offer a position in a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2) of this title to each applicant or recipient who—
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii) eligibility for an additional allocation (src:2149)
GIVEN `the State agency has made a commitment to offer a position in a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2) to each applicant or recipient described in subclauses (I) to (IV)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency complies with the commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii) the State agency is eligible for an additional allocation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has made a commitment to offer a position in a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2) to each applicant or recipient described in subclauses (I) to (IV)` AND `the State agency complies with the commitment` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible for an additional allocation under clause (i), a State agency shall make and comply with a commitment to offer a position"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2150 | (I) is in the last month of the 3-month period described in section 2015(o)(2) of this title;
-- src:2151 | (II) is not eligible for an exception under section 2015(o)(3) of this title;
-- src:2152 | (III) is not eligible for a waiver under section 2015(o)(4) of this title; and
-- src:2153 | (IV) is not exempt under section 2015(o)(6) of this title.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii)(I)-(IV) the applicants and recipients the commitment covers (src:2150-2153)
GIVEN `s 2015(o)(2) the individual is in the last month of the 3-month period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(o)(3) the individual is eligible for an exception` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(o)(4) the individual is eligible for a waiver` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(o)(6) the individual is exempt` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii) the commitment to offer a position covers the applicant or recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2015(o)(2) the individual is in the last month of the 3-month period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 2015(o)(3) the individual is eligible for an exception` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `s 2015(o)(4) the individual is eligible for a waiver` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `s 2015(o)(6) the individual is exempt` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the commitment is "to each applicant or recipient who" "is in the last month of the 3-month period", "is not eligible for an exception", "is not eligible for a waiver" and "is not exempt"; or an answer of section 2015(o) was not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(h)(2) to (5) Funding of employment and training programs: additional costs, reimbursement, use, monitoring`

-- "subject to the first limitation in paragraph (3)" is read as the cap on the reimbursement for dependent care expenses (fork F-9 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2279 | (2) If, in carrying out such program during such fiscal year, a State agency incurs costs that exceed the amount allocated to the State agency under paragraph (1), the Secretary shall pay such State agency an amount equal to 50 per centum of such additional costs, subject to the first limitation in paragraph (3), including the costs for case management and casework to facilitate the transition from economic dependency to self-sufficiency through work.
@ref s 2025(h)(2) 50 per centum of additional costs (src:2279)
GIVEN `costs incurred exceed the amount allocated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `additional costs other than dependent care expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `additional dependent care expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the most the reimbursement for dependent care expenses may be, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(2) the amount the Secretary shall pay for the additional costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `costs incurred exceed the amount allocated` THEN JUST ((`additional costs other than dependent care expenses, in dollars` TIMES 0.50) PLUS (min (`additional dependent care expenses, in dollars` TIMES 0.50) `the most the reimbursement for dependent care expenses may be, in dollars`))
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, in carrying out such program during such fiscal year, a State agency incurs costs that exceed the amount allocated to the State agency under paragraph (1)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2280 | (3) The Secretary shall also reimburse each State agency in an amount equal to 50 per centum of the total amount of payments made or costs incurred by the State agency in connection with transportation costs and other expenses reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in an employment and training program under section 2015(d)(4) of this title or a pilot project under paragraph (1)(F), except that the amount of the reimbursement for dependent care expenses shall not exceed an amount equal to the payment made under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) of this title but not more than the applicable local market rate, and such reimbursement shall not be made out of funds allocated under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2025(h)(3) the first limitation: dependent care (src:2280)
GIVEN `payment made under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `applicable local market rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(3) the most the reimbursement for dependent care expenses may be` MEANS
    min `payment made under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), in dollars` `applicable local market rate, in dollars`

@ref s 2025(h)(3) 50 per centum of payments made or costs incurred (src:2280)
GIVEN `payments and costs for transportation and other expenses other than dependent care, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `dependent care expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the most the reimbursement for dependent care expenses may be, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(h)(3) the amount the Secretary shall reimburse the State agency` MEANS
    (`payments and costs for transportation and other expenses other than dependent care, in dollars` TIMES 0.50) PLUS (min (`dependent care expenses, in dollars` TIMES 0.50) `the most the reimbursement for dependent care expenses may be, in dollars`)

@ref s 2025(h)(3) not out of funds allocated under paragraph (1) (src:2280)
GIVEN `the reimbursement is one made under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(3) the reimbursement may be made out of funds allocated under paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such reimbursement shall not be made out of funds allocated under paragraph (1)"
        IF `the reimbursement is one made under this paragraph` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "such reimbursement"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2281 | (4) Funds provided to a State agency under this subsection may be used only for operating an employment and training program under section 2015(d)(4) of this title or a pilot project under paragraph (1)(F), and may not be used for carrying out other provisions of this chapter.
@ref s 2025(h)(4) use of the funds (src:2281)
GIVEN `the use is operating an employment and training program under section 2015(d)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is operating a pilot project under paragraph (1)(F)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(4) the funds may be used for the use` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the use is operating an employment and training program under section 2015(d)(4)` OR `the use is operating a pilot project under paragraph (1)(F)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be used only for operating an employment and training program under section 2015(d)(4) of this title or a pilot project under paragraph (1)(F), and may not be used for carrying out other provisions of this chapter"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2284 | The Secretary shall monitor the employment and training programs carried out by State agencies under section 2015(d)(4) of this title and assess the effectiveness of the programs in—
-- src:2285 | (i) preparing members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for employment, including the acquisition of basic skills necessary for employment; and
-- src:2286 | (ii) increasing the number of household members who obtain and retain employment subsequent to participation in the employment and training programs.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(A) monitoring (src:2284-2286)
GIVEN `the Secretary monitors the employment and training programs carried out by State agencies under section 2015(d)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary assesses their effectiveness in preparing members of households for employment and in increasing the number who obtain and retain employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(A) the Secretary has monitored and assessed as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary monitors the employment and training programs carried out by State agencies under section 2015(d)(4)` AND `the Secretary assesses their effectiveness in preparing members of households for employment and in increasing the number who obtain and retain employment` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall monitor the employment and training programs carried out by State agencies under section 2015(d)(4) of this title and assess the effectiveness of the programs"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2289 | The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Labor, shall develop State reporting measures that identify improvements in the skills, training, education, or work experience of members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- src:2290 | (ii) Requirements.—
-- src:2291 | Measures shall—
-- src:2292 | (I) be based on common measures of performance for Federal workforce training programs; and
-- src:2293 | (II) include additional indicators that reflect the challenges facing the types of members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program who participate in a specific employment and training component.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(B)(i)-(ii) State reporting measures (src:2289-2293)
GIVEN `the Secretary develops the measures in consultation with the Secretary of Labor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they identify improvements in the skills, training, education, or work experience of members of households` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are based on common measures of performance for Federal workforce training programs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include additional indicators that reflect the challenges facing the types of members who participate in a specific component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(B) the State reporting measures are as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary develops the measures in consultation with the Secretary of Labor`
            AND `they identify improvements in the skills, training, education, or work experience of members of households`
            AND `they are based on common measures of performance for Federal workforce training programs`
            AND `they include additional indicators that reflect the challenges facing the types of members who participate in a specific component`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Labor, shall develop State reporting measures"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2295 | The Secretary shall require that each State employment and training plan submitted under section 2020(e)(19) of this title identifies appropriate reporting measures for each proposed component that serves a threshold number of participants determined by the Secretary of at least 100 people a year.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iii) the threshold of at least 100 people a year (src:2295)
GIVEN `threshold number of participants the Secretary determines, a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iii) the threshold the Secretary determines is allowed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `threshold number of participants the Secretary determines, a year` AT LEAST 100 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a threshold number of participants determined by the Secretary of at least 100 people a year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iii) each proposed component that serves a threshold number (src:2295)
GIVEN `participants the component serves, a year` IS A NUMBER
      `threshold number of participants the Secretary determines, a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iii) the State employment and training plan must identify reporting measures for the component` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `participants the component serves, a year` AT LEAST `threshold number of participants the Secretary determines, a year` AND `threshold number of participants the Secretary determines, a year` AT LEAST 100 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each proposed component that serves a threshold number of participants"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2297 | Reporting measures described in clause (iii) may include—
-- src:2298 | (I) the percentage and number of program participants who received employment and training services and are in unsubsidized employment subsequent to the receipt of those services;
-- src:2299 | (II) the percentage and number of program participants who obtain a recognized credential, including a registered apprenticeship, or a regular secondary school diploma or its recognized equivalent, while participating in, or within 1 year after receiving, employment and training services;
-- src:2300 | (III) the percentage and number of program participants who are in an education or training program that is intended to lead to a recognized credential, including a registered apprenticeship or on-the-job training program, a regular secondary school diploma or its recognized equivalent, or unsubsidized employment;
-- src:2301 | (IV) subject to terms and conditions established by the Secretary, measures developed by each State agency to assess the skills acquisition of employment and training program participants that reflect the goals of the specific employment and training program components of the State agency, which may include, at a minimum—
-- src:2302 | (aa) the percentage and number of program participants who are meeting program requirements in each component of the education and training program of the State agency;
-- src:2303 | (bb) the percentage and number of program participants who are gaining skills likely to lead to employment as measured through testing, quantitative or qualitative assessment, or other method; and
-- src:2304 | (cc) the percentage and number of program participants who do not comply with employment and training requirements and who are ineligible under section 2015(b) of this title; and
-- src:2305 | (V) other indicators approved by the Secretary.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) the measures that may be included (src:2297-2305)
GIVEN measure IS A `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) the reporting measure may be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER measure
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Reporting measures described in clause (iii) may include" the five listed
    WHEN `s 2025(h)(5)(B)(iv) any other measure` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2307 | The State agency may report relevant data from a workforce partnership carried out under section 2015(d)(4)(N) of this title to demonstrate the number of program participants served by the workforce partnership.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(B)(v) State option (src:2307)
GIVEN `the data are relevant data from a workforce partnership carried out under section 2015(d)(4)(N)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(B)(v) the State agency may report the data to demonstrate the number of participants served` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the data are relevant data from a workforce partnership carried out under section 2015(d)(4)(N)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relevant data from a workforce partnership carried out under section 2015(d)(4)(N)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2309 | The Secretary shall assess State employment and training programs on a periodic basis to ensure—
-- src:2310 | (i) compliance with Federal employment and training program rules and regulations;
-- src:2311 | (ii) that program activities are appropriate to meet the needs of the individuals referred by the State agency to an employment and training program component;
-- src:2312 | (iii) that reporting measures are appropriate to identify improvements in skills, training, work and experience for participants in an employment and training program component; and
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(C)(i)-(iii) oversight of State employment and training activities (src:2309-2312)
GIVEN `the Secretary assesses the State programs on a periodic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to ensure compliance with Federal employment and training program rules and regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to ensure that program activities are appropriate to meet the needs of the individuals referred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to ensure that reporting measures are appropriate to identify improvements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(C) the Secretary has assessed the State programs as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary assesses the State programs on a periodic basis`
            AND `to ensure compliance with Federal employment and training program rules and regulations`
            AND `to ensure that program activities are appropriate to meet the needs of the individuals referred`
            AND `to ensure that reporting measures are appropriate to identify improvements`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall assess State employment and training programs on a periodic basis to ensure"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2313 | (iv) for States receiving additional allocations under paragraph (1)(E), any information the Secretary may require to evaluate the compliance of the State agency with paragraph (1), which may include—
-- src:2314 | (I) a report for each fiscal year of the number of individuals in the State who meet the conditions of paragraph (1)(E)(ii), the number of individuals the State agency offers a position in a program described in subparagraph (B) or (C) of section 2015(o)(2) of this title, and the number who participate in such a program;
-- src:2315 | (II) a description of the types of employment and training programs the State agency uses to comply with paragraph (1)(E) and the availability of those programs throughout the State; and
-- src:2316 | (III) any additional information the Secretary determines to be appropriate.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) States receiving additional allocations (src:2313-2316)
GIVEN `the State receives additional allocations under paragraph (1)(E)` IS A BOOLEAN
      information IS A `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) the Secretary may require the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for States receiving additional allocations under paragraph (1)(E)"
        IF (NOT `the State receives additional allocations under paragraph (1)(E)`) THEN NOTHING
        IF information EQUALS `s 2025(h)(5)(C)(iv) any other information` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2318 | Each State agency shall annually prepare and submit to the Secretary a report on the State employment and training program that includes, using measures identified under subparagraph (B), the numbers of supplemental nutrition assistance program participants who have gained skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(D) State report (src:2318)
GIVEN `the State agency prepares and submits a report every year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it gives, using the measures identified, the numbers of participants who have gained skills, training, work, or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(D) the State agency has reported as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency prepares and submits a report every year` AND `it gives, using the measures identified, the numbers of participants who have gained skills, training, work, or experience` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each State agency shall annually prepare and submit to the Secretary a report on the State employment and training program"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2320 | Subject to terms and conditions established by the Secretary, if the Secretary determines that the performance of a State agency with respect to employment and training outcomes is inadequate, the Secretary may require the State agency to make modifications to the State employment and training plan to improve the outcomes.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(E) modifications to the State employment and training plan (src:2320)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the performance of the State agency with respect to employment and training outcomes is inadequate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(E) the Secretary may require the State agency to modify the plan` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that the performance of the State agency with respect to employment and training outcomes is inadequate`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines that the performance of a State agency with respect to employment and training outcomes is inadequate"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2322 | Subject to terms and conditions established by the Secretary, not later than October 1, 2016, and not less frequently than once every 5 years thereafter, the Secretary shall conduct a study to review existing practice and research to identify employment and training program components and practices that—
-- src:2323 | (i) effectively assist members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment; and
-- src:2324 | (ii) are best integrated with statewide workforce development systems.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(F) periodic evaluation (src:2322-2324)
GIVEN `date of the previous study, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date of the study` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(F) the study is conducted in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the previous study, if any`
    WHEN JUST previous THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `date of the study` AT MOST (`add years` previous 5) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than October 1, 2016, and not less frequently than once every 5 years thereafter"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `date of the study` AT MOST (Date 1 10 2016) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than October 1, 2016"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2322 | Subject to terms and conditions established by the Secretary, not later than October 1, 2016, and not less frequently than once every 5 years thereafter, the Secretary shall conduct a study to review existing practice and research to identify employment and training program components and practices that—
-- src:2323 | (i) effectively assist members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment; and
-- src:2324 | (ii) are best integrated with statewide workforce development systems.
@ref s 2025(h)(5)(F)(i)-(ii) what the study identifies (src:2322-2324)
GIVEN `the study reviews existing practice and research` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies employment and training program components and practices that effectively assist members of households in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies employment and training program components and practices that are best integrated with statewide workforce development systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(5)(F) the study covers what the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the study reviews existing practice and research`
            AND `it identifies employment and training program components and practices that effectively assist members of households in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment`
            AND `it identifies employment and training program components and practices that are best integrated with statewide workforce development systems`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall conduct a study to review existing practice and research to identify employment and training program components and practices that"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
